course: dictionary
lesson: 10691
title: Unrest, a word for trouble that won't settle
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unrest means a state of trouble, where people are angry, worried or unsettled. It is a noun you cannot count, so you say «some unrest», never «an unrest» or «unrests».
explain: The news often uses «civil unrest», and the context tells you what it means: riots and protests. When a country has unrest, people are upset and may take to the streets. Ask yourself: would a calm, peaceful town have unrest? No, so unrest means trouble.
explain: Unrest can also be a feeling inside you. In «a sweet unrest», the restless feeling is stirring, like excitement or longing that will not settle. Check your meaning by swapping in worry or trouble that won't settle, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Unrest is an uncountable noun, so do not add a or s to it.
fact: «Unrest» means trouble, when people are angry, unhappy or restless.
fact: «Civil unrest» means riots and protests among the people of a country.
fact: Phrases you may meet include «political unrest», «social unrest» and «unrest among the workers».
fact: Unrest can also mean a feeling of worry or restlessness that won't settle.
exercise: «Civil unrest» means which of these? | *Riots and protests | A quiet, peaceful holiday | A type of sleep | A kind of weather
exercise: The news says there is «unrest in the streets». What does this tell the reader? | *The place is troubled and may be unsafe | The streets have just been cleaned | The shops are all having sales | Everyone is asleep
exercise: Which sentence uses unrest correctly? | An unrest began on Monday | *There was unrest in the city all week | The unrests were quiet | There were three unrests in the city
test:
In «a sweet unrest», what does unrest mean? | Trouble and riots in the streets | *A restless feeling that will not settle | A deep, peaceful sleep | A sudden loud noise
Which phrase means riots and protests among the people of a country? | Social dinner | Unrest in the sea | *Civil unrest | Quiet afternoon
exam:
In «political unrest», which word is the best synonym for unrest? | Calm | Joy | *Trouble | Sleep
